#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198053 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ea202ce3-07d4-5324-9ee4-f5617b430772" :question/math-academy-id "e-12477" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R,$ defined as\n\n![](images/d8/d8be5d5bd5fa2cd8b618087109678a4f891b08f3788d4946d07bc1b5e4b39a3a.png)\n\ncalculate $\\boldsymbol f'$ at ![](images/a2/a2dbcf34ea50e451efc96ad2f9a7422a7ae507ca8f74088569110abb25293954.png)" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/17/17588b058b1e1fe934e06679836234f0ef35fe4484a558fcc3ec3b2aafbd2620.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol f$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol f$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/61/613ba027e9564812a8e050efd69fd98fff3f614f7d2ec69eeb787c628ccabd12.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/87/87579b882ca6d8c92d4a7adfed575873fd07c36ab20251722c2cc8fc0f0328e8.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)=2xy, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/9f/9fc2431aa874c68b23b6640da987b2f3bc37e2261936f7e1656b04bc3fc0030d.png)\n\nand $\\boldsymbol{f}'$ at ![](images/b8/b83c8f9cb4130103d63821f0d0de50ec0628138dcc8faaf16e8cf9fc27f1a994.png) is\n\n![](images/08/0851481c21c553b6e0e06a795815b1845e96e0a14f805e440529d0f4d6f85323.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198054 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198412 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ea76d21f-eff8-5634-975f-2b5bd24caf54" :question/math-academy-id "e-12478" :question/problem "For the transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R^3,$ defined as\n\n![](images/9f/9fb4fd5dfb788d65cc7ea3fd67bce06097c24e03454c3bd0c2971a4c24789f98.png)\n\nthe total derivative $\\boldsymbol f'$ is given by \n\n![](images/e5/e5100618308bb9c2d07f0a022c18da152d88f30a3c7f3e0e1e173e9d743ff278.png)\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/f1/f1c18d26fb7b6f1969bcda14d71ac18429466b4be8847097f227cdc537fdc8d9.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/4b/4b752e33d4ca3154590a5dc16ec3addd1d45a9618c92283903ff33d3818b8266.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/d1/d10e552c42ff8fe0df517b6297582bd5eeefdf29896a51005c79bd399a363c13.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=x, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})=2y, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{y}{x},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/8c/8c2cef2ba5322cc545860caa4d2f503f5f48a3374cce7c0f1e910a56f0357a64.png)\nThus, the missing entries are $y,\\:$ $0,\\:$ and $\\ln{x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198055 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198413 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "db0be438-94fe-52de-9daf-60d1727ce7b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12479" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R,$ defined as\n\n![](images/d1/d18d3d4b6ce4dc901608a0c8b91b245aa8922ad950d7b664b4de8320aa3c0818.png)\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at ![](images/62/62277cb0f04f6106a3039c916f28fbdf561bfdba6e08d576f1ed906b973ad90d.png) is given by\n\n![](images/d2/d2fcbb3375b9efa65559ba261581cf349dc801b3d84be5b465c36a7f4027c556.png)\n\nfind the missing values." :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/e7/e79145a13ada389ac337a69f8c48952f53b70d5caf48d950b305275ed8773b44.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/a4/a4de8e3eca77241030facac81ea44493400e00e34d1c7dde9ee9b25eab8441b0.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/5e/5ee75b93739a5018486c6b65a5e5c996f95b7f8ea6fdf6bd68b5727742e770fa.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})=3{x}^{2},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})={e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/a8/a8fd9120b29337c656c9b715bfa38dbecc7755e50877fad9719de54ed248a8ed.png)\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at ![](images/44/445be7536a39ee9c8d90f4cee571bf46acb5c995a9b53547f1aa582bd351592a.png) we have\n\n![](images/44/44faf9caacb8100249410ce233429c030fc52656be35c31d22f423397288da03.png)\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - f(\\mathbf a) = \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(\\mathbf a),$ $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a),$ and $\\mathbf a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n![](images/58/5824c66708813f59e2920287d35500ea68356ead4a4c3673d8807a0b81ca1abe.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198056 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198414 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f3540571-9159-50b4-a46c-4cf28a454602" :question/math-academy-id "e-12484" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R^2,$ defined as\n\n![](images/27/27a38861d0d2b0a8be98704202927c7a0dc0c638d11f25733b5a1e24faa18de2.png)\n\nIf the linear approximation of $\\boldsymbol f$ at ![](images/fa/fafc23364eb261c2d42baebfee5aec21491567c7c8d7cdbeb5c1f5c6c9d30ae8.png) is given by\n\n![](images/b8/b86418e6cd8fdf247d775882927c1a9d7a6e0cd392f8bd79b93e6b58f267fef7.png)\n\nwhat are the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/eb/eb248ccd80e8a10edab9d44c4cb11841aad35f6d35a778ff828607a312fcad35.png) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/47/47d512d278eaa912a112e96406e44d8b9a464984487e0ab9ff253a233441c2e1.png)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/4b/4bb0fb226d008d5efe2e7a04a444a2313b2acf80f71589a2aa0a17e40246c03b.png)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1})={x}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{1},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/9e/9eb84e24979469e9b1618f0a20f030963741a513292699ed4c4d342cd9d8e00d.png)\n\nEvaluating $\\boldsymbol{f}$ and its derivative at ![](images/22/22f4d34b8ec830740b285e1c31954b1e382264c4f366d3ea426ecadd3fd5f5bb.png) we have\n\n![](images/65/651b14a10334bdfc073b86359ce306c1b4ba25b9390f345b609978e34cc08cad.png)\n\nThe linear approximation of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}\\left(\\mathbf x \\right) \\approx \\boldsymbol{f}(\\mathbf a) + \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\boldsymbol{f}(\\mathbf a),$ $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a),$ and $\\mathbf a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n![](images/a0/a00401d8a9246532f363238c37646a6640a904db7f53d165d4f29c07e0a81a01.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198412 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be619527-6485-599f-b13d-4c3d1f82b137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2xyz$, $\\frac{1}{y}$, and $yz$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194430} {:answer/id #uuid "e07ccc1d-7a0d-51b4-83ae-4bd63ea88e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x^{2}y$, $\\frac{1}{z}$, and $x^{2}y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194431} {:answer/id #uuid "f49531ac-2637-58b2-b3eb-518cbd31db3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2xyz$, $\\frac{1}{z}$, and $y^{2}z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194432} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0d9b03-15d3-5ffc-aabc-a82ac6ce2655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x^{2}y$, $\\frac{1}{x}$, and $x^{2}y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194433} {:answer/id #uuid "48bbfa67-2e0d-585e-9f6e-f2bd8e316f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2xyz$, $\\frac{1}{y}$, and $x^{2}y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194434}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d21567a5-5f65-5300-b094-9bc5b4d4fdfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194429}] :question/id #uuid "d8b4c68b-51c3-543e-a36a-3adc1afaee33" :question/math-academy-id "q-162942" :question/problem "For the transformation $f: R^{3} → R^{2}$, defined as\n\n$f(x) = \\begin{bmatrix}\\ln (xyz) \\\\ x^{2}yz\\end{bmatrix}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}$,\n\nthe total derivative $f^{′}$ is given by\n\n$f^{′}(x) = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{x} & A A & \\frac{1}{z} \\\\ A A & x^{2}z & A A\\end{bmatrix}$.\nFrom left to right, what are the missing entries?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b80b86-64bb-54d9-a6ca-b27a6eaebca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367764} {:answer/id #uuid "3c49bd99-3471-511b-957a-8ab3b1903bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367765} {:answer/id #uuid "94531792-a246-55d0-95b4-9f8194bd82a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367766} {:answer/id #uuid "715f6f02-e6fb-5ed3-ad0c-c279c3b1e987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367767} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b636fa-6aba-526b-9de7-3981175973af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11b80b86-64bb-54d9-a6ca-b27a6eaebca6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367764} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f8006a8-9366-5d6f-ae22-58b3ac1b10e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8b2963e-d3c7-59db-be98-15648e5aba5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163048" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=x{y}^{2}-y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}-y)={y}^{2}, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}-y)=2xy-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & 2xy-1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}(1)^{2} & 2(0)(1)-1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198413 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f0af6f4-8846-5cc9-b0d0-ef675db7ecfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194550} {:answer/id #uuid "93e51430-7515-5ea7-b676-8718aa40b834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194551} {:answer/id #uuid "f248937d-3d19-5f99-a0d4-d58ced4eba66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194552} {:answer/id #uuid "15e93809-1fc8-5035-b5b6-cb4d0ca11d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194553} {:answer/id #uuid "263c53e8-2f06-5be5-9f6a-884b62308d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194554}] :answer-field/id #uuid "dbabfec0-d273-5628-a4d6-fe7beb8d8851" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194549}] :question/id #uuid "1286acb9-42cc-5da3-a992-0e5c7b3d2c79" :question/math-academy-id "q-163057" :question/problem "Consider the function $f: R^{2} → R$, defined as\n\n$f(x) = e^{x} + y, x = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is given by\n\n$z - ∗ = \\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}(\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix})$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198413 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa2eb46-7da9-5a93-ab46-905177cc8d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367792} {:answer/id #uuid "20e67f4c-0912-57d9-b100-79cfe229487b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367793} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d766a7-f722-54d5-a4bd-8afd2c4dbcfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367794} {:answer/id #uuid "c70eb82d-5858-5ea5-af10-6241b5f04e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367795} {:answer/id #uuid "2e4cae0c-20a3-51e2-90c3-75d418d9f057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c70eb82d-5858-5ea5-af10-6241b5f04e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367795} :answer-field/id #uuid "1db7e5b9-cbc0-5e13-8675-3951d7667a88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08e9a1c4-09e3-536e-9e2b-e51736b93226" :question/math-academy-id "q-163074" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{xy+1},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{xy+1})=-\\frac{y}{(xy+1)^{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{xy+1})=-\\frac{x}{(xy+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y}{(xy+1)^{2}} & -\\frac{x}{(xy+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-\\frac{1}{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{1}{4})+(-\\frac{1}{4})=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198414 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d2eba0c-14d4-56fe-8ab5-619751969660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367799} {:answer/id #uuid "7503905e-9b4f-5407-8c01-413a7b68830f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367800} {:answer/id #uuid "21f31c1f-b694-556a-98db-778605e79743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367801} {:answer/id #uuid "8433daa5-6e2c-55ec-b2e3-edef5e21a44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367802} {:answer/id #uuid "f01146e8-4036-5342-a70e-9a2652f1ab42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d2eba0c-14d4-56fe-8ab5-619751969660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367799} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a050f39-aa59-5d92-be17-99b992f19596" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "89e6f405-4017-5664-a468-c2ee8d215a47" :question/math-academy-id "q-163083" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at  $a=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4} \\\\ ∗\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & -1\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2})=1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2})=2{x}_{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}),\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2{x}_{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\pi  \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\pi  \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+\\pi +(-1)=\\pi -1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198412 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d959d5d7-cbc1-5318-b797-c37a0afbbf37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401414} {:answer/id #uuid "b30dc2cc-68a4-5912-8a3e-df5e08613c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${e}^{xyz},\\,$ $2x,\\,$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401415} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd45803-73b4-58a2-b054-1d9f41e88d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$yz{e}^{yz},\\,$ $0,\\,$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401416} {:answer/id #uuid "43123342-28a0-58f0-8627-2ed0371a4ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$yz{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401417} {:answer/id #uuid "1c151508-a070-5be8-9646-29a3b6c0d0e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43123342-28a0-58f0-8627-2ed0371a4ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$yz{e}^{xyz},\\,$ $z,\\,$ and $y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401417} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cbe7815-5a90-5779-9948-27720bbf467a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e4436f3f-18fe-5775-815d-04fe166d17a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163100" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{xyz} \\\\ x+yz\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} & xz{e}^{xyz} & xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ 1 & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing entries?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xyz})=yz{e}^{xyz},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xyz})=xz{e}^{xyz},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{xyz})=xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+yz)=1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+yz)=z,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x+yz)=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}yz{e}^{xyz} & xz{e}^{xyz} & xy{e}^{xyz} \\\\ 1 & z & y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198414 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc8f2d1-ecfb-50d7-b14b-04f9786d82ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367834} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7d0746-3536-5992-9206-08d262d180df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367835} {:answer/id #uuid "64ad6963-dfe5-5f16-bbef-d203883d7998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367836} {:answer/id #uuid "566980c0-9d00-5a29-b05a-cac367edfbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367837} {:answer/id #uuid "dc697d16-cd1d-50e1-81a4-0a7ea90187b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64ad6963-dfe5-5f16-bbef-d203883d7998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367836} :answer-field/id #uuid "703aea1e-c64a-581f-b4f6-a53c00907653" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b78101c4-fecc-5cba-9eee-2c628a3b3929" :question/math-academy-id "q-163162" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{3}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}}\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}∗ \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{1}^{3}-{x}_{2})=3{x}_{1}^{2},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{1}^{3}-{x}_{2})=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}})={e}^{{x}_{1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}^{2} & -1 \\\\ {x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}} & {e}^{{x}_{1}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+(-1)+1=1.\n$$"}]}
